n\n### What remains to be done\n\n1. **Edit `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`**: append under `parent=\"Level\"`:\n   - `[node name=\"CoinHighlights\" type=\"Node2D\" parent=\"Level\"]`\n   - Six `Polygon2D` nodes named `CoinHighlight1`…`CoinHighlight6`, each with a circular polygon (e.g., 24 points covering a full circle of radius ~13–14 in Level-local/texture coordinates, centered at the coin centers listed above — e.g., `polygon = PackedVector2Array(425.5+13·cos θ, 71.5+13·sin θ, ...)`) and a semi-transparent color, e.g. `color = Color(1, 1, 0, 0.5)`. Place each highlight after the Sprite2D (or set `z_index`) so it renders on top.\n2. **Verify visually**: run `timeout 10 godot --path . --quit-after 1 --write-movie verify.png` from `/workspace`, open the produced PNG, and confirm six semi-transparent circles tightly cover the six coins with minimal spill; adjust centers/radii if needed.\n\n### Recommended next step (single concrete edit)\n\nRewrite `scenes/main.tscn` adding the `CoinHighlights` Node2D and six circular-segment `Polygon2D` children using the centers/radii above (generated at full precision via the cosine/sine lists), then render one frame and visually check alignment.","time":{"start":1790457633643,"end":1790457633647},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_chatcmpl-6ab83722201bb9e45bfef9c3_msg"}}}}
